        "caption": "Boris Cherny built Claude Code, then turned it on himself.\n\nUsing a feature he calls loops, cron-scheduled Claude sessions now run around the clock, five to ten parallel sessions with hundreds of agents during the day, thousands overnight, all managed mostly from his phone.\n\nSome loops auto-fix Cl issues and rebase pull requests. Others catch flaky tests or scan Twitter, GitHub, Discord, and support channels every 30 minutes to surface patterns in feedback.\n\nThe result: 20 to 30 pull requests shipped daily, and every one of his last 150 PRs was written entirely by Claude. His latest addition, Routines, moves the same system server-side so it keeps working even after he closes his laptop.\n\nThe guy who built Claude Code basically built himself an engineering team that never sleeps.\n\nMedia: Alex Kantrowitz/YT\n\n#claudecode\n\n#anthropic\n\n#aiagents",
