          {
            "id": "18094733351554914",
            "text": "One tactic I've been using: speech-to-text brain dumps with the agent. I just talk it out, literally stream of consciousness, then ask it to distill and summarize that into something coherent I can review. From there, we discuss it together and refine it. whether it's a feature, greenfield, brownfield, a bug, a POC, or an MVP, that's always the starting point. I keep using that same brain dump → distill → summarize loop as the work continues.\n\nNo fancy skills involved. Just two documents: a handoff doc and a session doc. The session doc captures what we did in that chat; the handoff doc carries forward anything specific Claude needs to know going into a new session , nothing else. That's enough to pick up in a fresh chat with no lost context, and it saves a lot of token burn since I'm not re-passing skills, MCP servers, or extra info I don't need.\n\nThe reasoning: your brain doesn't work by holding everything in context. It pattern-matches on the task at hand and pulls only what's relevant from long-term memory. This setup mirrors that.",
